# What never enters a build context.
#
# Two jobs, and the second is the one people forget. The obvious one is image size. The
# other is the developer inner loop: `docker compose watch` (ADR-0018) walks this same
# tree, so anything left in here is something the host-side watcher has to stat on every
# save — and `thoughts/` alone is hundreds of files that could never change a build.
#
# Rule of thumb: if COPY in a Dockerfile does not name it, it does not belong here.

# Dependencies. Built for darwin-arm64 on this machine and for linux in the image; letting
# the host's copy into the context is how "works on my machine" gets containerised.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. Regenerated inside the image; a stale local copy would silently win.
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# Version control and CI metadata. The build args carry the git SHA (ADR-0011); the image
# has no reason to contain the history it came from.
.git
.gitignore
.githooks
.github

# Local configuration and secrets. `.env` is the one file that must never be baked in: the
# container takes its configuration from compose, and an image carrying a developer's
# environment is an image that behaves differently everywhere else (ADR-0009).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The written record. Large, and none of it is code.
thoughts
docs
mockups

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
*.log

# The compose files and load scripts are read by the docker CLI, not copied into an image.
infra
